                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Psalm 127 The Need of God’s Blessing - A song of ascents. Of Solomon. I - Unless the LORD build the house, they labor in vain who build. Unless the LORD guard the city, in vain does the guard keep watch.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "2",
                       "number":  2,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "It is vain for you to rise early and put off your rest at night, To eat bread earned by hard toil— all this God gives to his beloved in sleep.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "3",
                       "number":  3,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "II - Certainly sons are a gift from the LORD, the fruit of the womb, a reward.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "4",
                       "number":  4,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Like arrows in the hand of a warrior are the sons born in one’s youth.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "5",
                       "number":  5,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Blessed is the man who has filled his quiver with them. He will never be shamed for he will destroy his foes at the gate.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   }
               ],
    "marks":  [

              ]
}